eived_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kulinseth/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kulinseth/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kulinseth/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kulinseth/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kulinseth","user_view_type":"public"},{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/122648248?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shuhand0/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shuhand0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shuhand0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shuhand0/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shuhand0","id":122648248,"login":"shuhand0","node_id":"U_kgDOB092uA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shuhand0/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shuhand0/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shuhand0/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shuhand0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shuhand0/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shuhand0","user_view_type":"public"}],"author_association":"NONE","body":"### Description\r\n\r\nWhen running the following program twice:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\r\n\r\nlogits = jnp.array([[-0.63927454,  0.0,         -1.2245101],\r\n [-0.17820558,  0.0,         -0.7477473]],      dtype=jnp.float32)\r\n\r\nlabels1 = jnp.array([[0, 1]])\r\nlabels2 = jnp.array([[1], [0]], dtype=jnp.int32)\r\n\r\nprint(jnp.take_along_axis(logits, labels1, axis=1))\r\nprint(jnp.take_along_axis(logits, labels2, axis=1))\r\n```\r\nIt produces different outputs:\r\n```\r\n(jax-metal)  ~/example > python3.11 err.py\r\n2024-06-10 06:25:40.053596: W pjrt_plugin/src/mps_client.cc:534] WARNING: JAX Apple GPU support is experimental and not all JAX functionality is correctly supported!\r\nMetal device set to: Apple M1\r\n\r\nsystemMemory: 8.00 GB\r\nmaxCacheSize: 2.67 GB\r\n\r\n[[-0.63927454  0.        ]\r\n [-0.17820558  0.        ]]\r\n[[ 0.        ]\r\n [-0.17820558]]\r\n(jax-metal)  ~/example > python3.11 err.py\r\n2024-06-10 06:25:43.420291: W pjrt_plugin/src/mps_client.cc:534] WARNING: JAX Apple GPU support is experimental and not all JAX functionality is correctly supported!\r\nMetal device set to: Apple M1\r\n\r\nsystemMemory: 8.00 GB\r\nmaxCacheSize: 2.67 GB\r\n\r\n[[-0.63927454  0.        ]\r\n [-0.17820558  0.        ]]\r\n[[ 0.]\r\n [nan]]\r\n```\r\n\r\nUsually has to be reran ~10 times in order to see the behavior change.\r\n\r\nThis behavior disappears when the program is run without accessing the array with `labels1` first:\r\n```python\r\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\r\n\r\nlogits = jnp.array([[-0.63927454,  0.0,         -1.2245101],\r\n [-0.17820558,  0.0,         -0.7477473]],      dtype=jnp.float32)\r\nlabels = jnp.array([[1], [0]], dtype=jnp.int32)\r\nprint(jnp.take_along_axis(logits, labels, axis=1))\r\n```\r\n\r\n### System info (python version, jaxlib version, accelerator, etc.)\r\n\r\n```\r\njax:    0.4.11\r\njaxlib: 0.4.11\r\nnumpy:  1.26.2\r\npython: 3.11.4 (main, Jul 25 2023, 17:36:13) [Clang 14.0.3 (clang-1403.0.22.14.1)]\r\njax.devices (1 total, 1 local): [MetalDevice(id=0, process_index=0)]\r\nprocess_count: 1\r\n```\r\nI'm using  MacOS 14.1.1 (23B81) with  `jax-metal==0.0.4`.","closed_at":"2026-01-20T18:43:46Z","comments":3,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/21757/comments","created_at":"2024-06-10T05:23:34Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/21757/events","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/21757","id":2342881472,"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"total_blocking":0},"issue_field_values":[],"labels":[{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"